  "body": "### Description\n\n\r\nWhen I create a new private room it displays:\r\n```\r\nname joined the room\r\nname made the room invite only.\r\nname made future room history visible to all room members.\r\nname has allowed guests to join the room.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe room is set to private, element is set to not allow guests, encryption is enabled.\r\n\r\nIt is telling me guests are **allowed**, so it is either a bug, I misunderstand, or I am missing a config setting. Registration is on but only allowed with token.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a new private and encrypted room using Synapse + element versions listed above.\r\n\n\n### Homeserver\n\nMy own homeserver\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n1.75.0+focal1\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDebian packages from packages.matrix.org\n\n### Database\n\nfresh postgresql (single on same machine as synapse)\n\n### Workers\n\nSingle process\n\n### Platform\n\nKVM VPS\r\nUbuntu 20\r\nElement 1.11.19 (on separate KVM VPS)\n\n### Configuration\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nNA\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\n_No response_",
